The committed module used getattr (4 dynamic-resolution sites), which
tripped TWO independent gates:
  * tests/egaie/test_orchestrator.py::test_package_has_no_dynamic_resolution
    (the egaie package forbids getattr outright), and
  * the G-02 direct-I/O inventory no-drift gate (dynamic-resolution
    sites are inventory records; the AST scan found 4 sites the
    recorded artifact did not carry).

Rewritten with explicit field access via dataclasses.asdict —
0 dynamic-resolution sites, inventory scan == artifact exactly
(1223 == 1223), 11/11 identity-scope tests + the no-dynamic-resolution
gate pass, ruff clean.
---
 .../src/webpent/egaie/identity_scope.py       | 56 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/WebPent_UNIFIED/src/webpent/egaie/identity_scope.py b/WebPent_UNIFIED/src/webpent/egaie/identity_scope.py
index 56ecbd8..1f1573f 100644
--- a/WebPent_UNIFIED/src/webpent/egaie/identity_scope.py
+++ b/WebPent_UNIFIED/src/webpent/egaie/identity_scope.py
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ from __future__ import annotations
 
